<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Indian Stream</h1><p class="st-meta">1832 CE – 1835 CE</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A tiny self-governing republic on the disputed border between New Hampshire and Lower Canada, home to about 300 settlers.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1783">Treaty of Paris</a> of 1783 set the border at the 'northwesternmost head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut-river">Connecticut River</a>', which could be read as several different streams. Settlers in the disputed valley found themselves taxed and called for service by both the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> and British <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lower-canada">Lower Canada</a>. In 1832 they adopted a constitution and declared their own republic.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Indian Stream was governed by an assembly of all adult male citizens, an elected council and its own courts, and it promised to last only until the boundary was settled. Its inhabitants were farmers and lumbermen. Divisions grew between residents loyal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-hampshire">New Hampshire</a> and those leaning to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-canada">Canada</a>, and an arrest by a New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hampshire">Hampshire</a> sheriff's deputy sparked clashes in 1835.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-hampshire">New Hampshire</a> sent militia in 1835 and annexed the territory in 1836. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/webster-ashburton-treaty">Webster-Ashburton Treaty</a> of 1842 confirmed it as American. The area is now the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pittsburg-new-hampshire">Pittsburg, New Hampshire</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-indian-stream.jpg" alt="Republic of Indian Stream" width="320" height="230"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Citynoise at English Wikipedia. Later versions were uploaded by AnonMoos at en.wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indian_stream_map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1832 CE – 1835 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestantism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Indian Stream Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1834&amp;focus=republic-of-indian-stream" aria-label="Republic of Indian Stream on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2984 584 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Indian Stream lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3304 840L2570 1008"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2570 1008h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3304 840h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3304 840h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1834&amp;focus=republic-of-indian-stream">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
